    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 50 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nI made `householdId` deterministic and reworked everything that keys off the household to use it.\n\n**`Households.java`** \u2014 Replaced the \"join an existing household only if `sharesHousehold`\" logic with a single deterministic function: `householdId(lastName, postcode)` = the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. Last name is lower-cased/whitespace-collapsed, postcode trimmed. It's never null. Removed the now-unused `resolve`/`sameHousehold` and the old address-based hash.\n\n**`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 Now unconditionally stamps `owner.setHouseholdId(Households.householdId(lastName, postcode))`. No opt-in, no back-filling \u2014 every owner (even a lone one) carries the computed id, so members converge on the same value independently.\n\n**`RejectDuplicateIdentity.java`** \u2014 Computes the request's `householdId` and rejects with 409 in two cases:\n- *Identity duplicate* \u2014 full `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) matches an existing owner. Always rejects, even with `sharesHousehold` (this is what keeps Cp28 a 409).\n- *Household duplicate* \u2014 an existing owner shares the computed `householdId` (same last name + postcode). Rejects **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold`, which now only bypasses this block.\n\n**`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 A declared household member (`sharesHousehold: true`) is no longer flagged as a possible duplicate; it short-circuits to `possibleDuplicate = false`. (Non-declared owners that would match are already blocked at 409, so the soft-match effectively never fires now.)\n\n**`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 No logic change needed (it already counts by stored `householdId`); I only refreshed the stale doc comment.\n\n## Behaviour, per the spec\n- Same last name + postcode \u2192 same `householdId` automatically (Cp11, Cp36).\n- A second such owner \u2192 409 household duplicate (Cp10, Cp35) unless it declares `sharesHousehold`, then it's created as a member and not flagged (Cp35).\n- Duplicate detection and household-size both key off the computed id (Cp03, Cp23, Cp25, Cp28).",
